<section class="shell band">
  <h1>Getting licensed as an LPC in Texas</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Full LPC licensure in Texas requires a qualifying graduate degree, two exams, an LPC
    Associate licence, and then <strong>3,000 clock-hours</strong> of supervised experience
    under a Council-approved supervisor. At least <strong>1,500</strong> of those hours must be
    direct client counselling contact, and the 3,000 cannot be completed in fewer than
    <strong>18 months</strong>. While you are accruing them you must receive at least
    <strong>four hours of supervision a month</strong>, with no more than half of your total
    supervision hours in a group. Your LPC Associate licence expires 60 months from issuance
    and cannot be renewed.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="source">Rules cited below are from 22 Texas Administrative Code, Chapter 681,
  administered by the <a href="https://bhec.texas.gov">Texas Behavioral Health Executive
  Council</a>. Current as of September 2026. Rules change, so verify anything you are about to
  rely on against BHEC directly.</p>
</section>

