<section class="shell band">
  <h2>Staying licensed, and becoming a supervisor</h2>
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h3>Continuing education</h3>
      <p>Full LPCs complete 24 hours of continuing education in each two-year renewal period,
      including at least 6 hours in ethics and 3 hours in cultural diversity and competency,
      plus an HHSC-approved human trafficking prevention course. Since 1 January 2024 at least
      half of the 24 hours must come from a provider listed in §681.140(f). You also pass the
      jurisprudence exam each renewal period, which counts as one hour of ethics credit.</p>
      <p><a href="/for-therapists/retreats-training/">Ethics CEUs and training with Reem</a></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Becoming an LPC-S</h3>
      <p>Supervisor status requires an unrestricted LPC licence in good standing for at least
      five years, plus either a 40-clock-hour supervision course meeting §681.147 or a
      for-credit doctoral-level course in supervision. Once approved, holding it requires 6
      hours of supervision-specific continuing education per renewal period, which count inside
      the 24.</p>
      <p>BHEC's current guidance says the supervision course does not expire once completed,
      while the rule text has historically referenced recency windows. If your certificate is
      old, confirm with BHEC before you apply.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Texas LPC licensure questions</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>How many supervised hours do you need for an LPC in Texas?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>3,000 clock-hours of supervised experience under a Council-approved supervisor, of
      which at least 1,500 must be direct client counselling contact. Only actual time spent
      counselling counts as direct. The 3,000 cannot be completed in fewer than 18 months, per
      22 TAC §681.92.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How many hours of supervision does an LPC Associate need each month?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>A minimum of four hours a month while you are counselling. Individual supervision means
      a supervisor with one or two associates; group means three or more. No more than 50% of
      your total supervision hours may be group. You can have up to two LPC supervisors on file
      at once.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How long does it take to become an LPC in Texas?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Eighteen months at the absolute fastest after you are licensed as an Associate,
      because that floor applies regardless of how quickly you accrue hours. At fifteen direct
      client hours a week it takes about two years; at eight a week, closer to three and a half.
      Add the two to three years of graduate study before that.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Does my LPC Associate licence expire?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes. It expires 60 months from the date of issuance and cannot be renewed. If you have
      not completed the required supervised experience in that window, you must reapply for
      licensure and meet the requirements in effect at the time of reapplication.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do hours count if I worked before getting my Associate licence?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. Hours obtained by an unlicensed person do not count toward the supervised
      experience requirement, in any setting. Get licensed first.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I do supervision online in Texas?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes. Texas rules set the amount and structure of supervision rather than requiring it
      to be in person, and online supervision is common across the state. Reem Glasco, LPC-S,
      supervises online only, which means associates anywhere in Texas can work with her.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What qualifies someone to supervise LPC Associates in Texas?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>An unrestricted Texas LPC licence in good standing for at least five years, plus a
      40-clock-hour supervision course meeting 22 TAC §681.147 or a for-credit doctoral-level
      course in supervision, and approval by BHEC as an LPC-S. Verify any supervisor's status on
      the BHEC licence lookup before signing an agreement.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>

